edit('docs/ci-and-builds.md', [('The current development package version is **1.8.0**; see [its release record](releases/release-1.8.0.md).', 'The current package version is **1.8.2**; see [its release record](releases/release-1.8.2.md).'), ('The [1.8.0 release notes](releases/release-1.8.0.md) describe current behavior', 'The [1.8.2 release notes](releases/release-1.8.2.md) describe current behavior'), ('exact unified 27-tool catalog', 'exact unified 28-tool catalog'), ('current 27-tool probe', 'current 28-tool probe'), ('The 17 prefixed native', 'The 18 prefixed native')])

path = root / 'docs/releases/release-1.8.2.md'
text = path.read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('# AIRK 1.8.2 candidate', '# AIRK 1.8.2 — installed responsiveness and conversational retrieval')
text = text.replace('Unpublished source candidate, 2026-11-01, on `feat/optimizations`.', 'Release record, 2026-11-01, prepared on `feat/optimizations`. Publication is verified separately through the protected release workflows.')
at = text.index('\n\nA finite conversational grammar')
text = text[:at] + '\n\n## More responsive installed startup and first status\n\nThe owner approved the 1.8.2 installation and reports quicker loading and previously slow or timed-out requests returning promptly. **All five fresh sessions through the actual installed launcher returned an available first status, with zero status timeouts.** Median initialization through confirmed status was **2.29 seconds**. The retained installed 1.7.6 example took about **5.5 seconds**, including a timed-out first status and a second request. The first new session took **7.31 seconds** and remains in the sample. Different corpora, background conditions and sample counts mean this is an observed improvement, not a controlled or guaranteed speedup percentage.\n\nThe changes address installed readiness, fenced verification reuse, independent status ownership, early verified UI health and selected-project preparation. Cold setup now has a separate bounded allowance; it no longer consumes the established status-observation deadline. Avoiding false timeouts is a reliability improvement as well as a better user experience. Explorer sends full Search results once instead of twice (**50% fewer deliveries**), and scalar status messages in the retained 200-turn Workbench fixture are **over 95% smaller**. Those percentages measure transfer work.\n\nThe [special performance report and causal analysis](../performance-improvements-1.8.2.md) explains why these installed/UI gains differ from isolated native indexing and retrieval measurements. It retains all native regressions, errors, outliers and unmeasured paths.\n\n## Conversational retrieval' + text[at:]
text = text.replace('## Installation handoff before the next corpus comparison', '## Historical installation handoff before final comparison')
text = text.replace('The requested order is:', 'At the earlier handoff, the requested order was:')
text = text.replace('No new corpus campaign is running at this checkpoint.', 'No new corpus campaign was running at that historical checkpoint.')
text = text.replace('Build/install authorization does not authorize publication.', 'The later owner acceptance and explicit release authorization below supersede that checkpoint.')
text = text.replace('Native activation in the existing normal window remains unverified until the user runs **Developer: Reload Window**. User manual acceptance remains pending, and no new corpus comparison has run.', 'That handoff awaited normal-profile Reload Window and manual acceptance. The owner subsequently confirmed that the 1.8.2 installation worked and approved it, then explicitly authorized the final comparison, commit, PR and release.')
text = text.replace('Publication is not authorized. The prior 1.8.1 evidence and retained native-boundary/corpus/platform failures remain identifiable. Targeted installed product assertions and native parse checks passed. Full installed-editor lifecycle and cross-platform qualification, normal-profile manual acceptance and elapsed-time performance qualification remain incomplete; publication is not authorized.', 'The owner approved the installed product and explicitly authorized commit, push, PR, publication and release on November 1. Earlier 1.8.1 and native-boundary/corpus/platform failures remain identifiable. The manual acceptance does not establish full installed lifecycle, cross-platform qualification or a general native speedup.')
text += '\n\n## Final matched corpus comparison and release checks\n\nThe 1.7.6 and 1.8.2 release pairs used identical source identities and native-default policies. AIRK reached full readiness in 50m 7.517s versus 52m 6.324s (3.95% longer); both versions completed 30 running-service and 30 reopen sessions. The 1.8.2 running-service cohort retained 14 native errors across 150 reads; 1.7.6 retained zero. Both reopen cohorts returned 150/150 usable reads. These explicit-service measurements bypass the installed launcher/editor startup path and support no general native retrieval speedup claim.\n\nBoth campaigns exited with `campaign_deadline` at BigDotNetProject’s unchanged one-hour semantic-readiness allowance: 1,024/8,121 completed artifacts for 1.7.6 and 768/8,121 for 1.8.2. Its later cohorts did not execute. Both graceful shutdown waits failed; owned reaping succeeded, and subsequent checks found no benchmark-owned processes or index fixture directories. A separate post-run check verified both complete source identities were unchanged and matched across versions before documentation edits. Raw receipts remain unchanged and private. See the [full performance report](../performance-improvements-1.8.2.md) for percentiles, first availability, failures, identities and causal-analysis limits.\n\nFinal local release checks: formatting and all-target/all-feature workspace Clippy passed; extension tests passed 506 with 18 skips; Python contracts passed 271 with six skips; release notices cover 366 packages; the fresh advisory gate passed with three existing reviewed exceptions and zero failures. The ordinary-root all-feature workspace run stopped at the three native-owner recovery cases with unavailable Windows private-boundary policy. A new protected temporary-directory attempt also refused that boundary; those cases are not passing coverage. Repository, version, privacy, review and hosted release results are recorded at handoff when observed.\n'
path.write_text(text, encoding='utf-8')

path = root / 'docs/optimizations.md'
text = path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
text = text.replace('## Current 1.8.0 scope — October 31, 2026 (America/Denver)', '## Historical 1.8.0 scope — October 31, 2026 (America/Denver)', 1)
intro = '**Current 1.8.2 outcome — November 1, 2026:** the owner approved the installed product and observed improved loading and request responsiveness. Five fresh installed-launcher sessions returned available first statuses with no timeouts; median initialization through confirmed status was 2.29 seconds, with the 7.31-second first-session outlier retained. The [performance report and causal analysis](performance-improvements-1.8.2.md) separates this primary installed experience from the matched explicit-service corpus campaign, its native regressions and readiness failures. Commit/PR/publication are explicitly authorized by the owner; earlier authorization restrictions below retain their historical scope.\n\n'
text = text.replace('\n\nTarget release:', '\n\n' + intro + 'Original target release:', 1)
start = text.index('**Current 1.8.2 handoff order:**')
end = text.index('\n\n', start)
text = text[:start] + '**1.8.2 handoff update:** normal-editor installation is owner-approved. The final matched corpus campaigns and installed-launcher observations have run; source preservation is verified. The owner explicitly authorized documentation, commit/push, PR and publication/release. The [report](performance-improvements-1.8.2.md) records installed responsiveness gains, native regressions and incomplete BigDotNetProject qualification; earlier handoff restrictions are superseded.' + text[end:]
text = text.replace('The user selected **`D:\\code\\github\\BigDotNetProject`** and **`D:\\code\\Github\\airk`** as the sizeable indexing/retrieval corpora.', 'The user selected the private corpus published under the alias **BigDotNetProject** and **AIRK** as the sizeable indexing/retrieval corpora. The private corpus location is intentionally omitted from public documentation; original local receipts retain the actual source identity.')
text = text.replace('Obtain a matched before/after comparison with recorded source/runtime/policy/environment identities.', 'The final matched before/after comparison is recorded in the performance report; it does not complete BigDotNetProject readiness or establish a general native speedup.')
text = text.replace('Current local build authorization does not authorize publication.', 'The November 1 owner direction explicitly authorizes commit, PR and publication after documentation and required release gates.')
text += '\n\n## Final 1.8.2 responsiveness and corpus comparison — November 1, 2026\n\nThe owner-approved installed experience is the primary responsiveness result. Five fresh configured-launcher sessions returned available first statuses without a timeout; median initialization through confirmed status was 2.29 seconds (first-session outlier 7.31 seconds). The retained 1.7.6 installed example took about 5.5 seconds including a timeout and a second status. This unmatched historical observation must not be presented as a controlled percentage.\n\nThe separate explicit-service comparison used identical captured sources across 1.7.6 and 1.8.2. It measured native regressions, retained 14 running-service read errors in 1.8.2, and hit BigDotNetProject’s one-hour semantic-readiness deadline in both versions. Both 30-session AIRK reopen cohorts returned all 150 requested reads. Graceful shutdown failures, successful owned reaping, final absence of owned processes/fixtures and independent unchanged-source verification remain distinct observations. See the [complete report and causal analysis](performance-improvements-1.8.2.md) for data, provenance, measurement coverage and the remaining optimization work.\n'
path.write_text(text, encoding='utf-8')
edit('docs/releases/README.md', [('- [1.8.2](./release-1.8.2.md) — unpublished source candidate: conversational evidence parsing, query-first Workbench reveal, expanded role training and included training data/fork guide', '- [1.8.2](./release-1.8.2.md) — installed startup/status responsiveness, conversational evidence parsing, query-first Workbench reveal, result selection/copy and [performance measurements/causal analysis](../performance-improvements-1.8.2.md); publication verified separately')])
